WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.984
Anika: Okay, the file descriptor limit pilot passed. Two staging workers now have higher limits.

2
00:00:06.984 --> 00:00:13.920
Lukas: Did you change the shell ulimit only? Systemd services inherit their own configured limits.

3
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:21.383
Anika: No, managed configuration sets the service limit. We checked the running process after restart.

4
00:00:21.383 --> 00:00:28.871
Hannah: Was the kernel-wide file table checked too? A higher per-process cap isn't free capacity.

5
00:00:28.871 --> 00:00:35.927
Raj: Yes, and memory headroom stayed healthy. The test also bounded connection counts explicitly.

6
00:00:35.927 --> 00:00:43.343
Priya: Just to confirm, production unchanged, right? Increasing limits doesn't fix a descriptor leak.

7
00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:51.071
Lukas: Correct, document the rollback trigger separately. Restore the saved service configuration if checks fail.

8
00:00:51.071 --> 00:00:57.430
Anika: And a restart needs its approved window. Roughly five minutes per worker in staging.

9
00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:05.158
Hannah: Don't copy that timing straight into production. Workload and draining behavior may differ there.

10
00:01:05.158 --> 00:01:12.790
Priya: So, production sizing? Let's park that. Today we finish the pilot evidence first.

